      "article_url": "https://www.npr.org/2026/10/18/nx-s1-6006805/will-ai-take-my-job-ask-an-economist",
      "image": "https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3377x1900+0+0/resize/1400/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd8%2Fe8%2F83ac358f46a69443d12d707b90a3%2F3fbf10dc-76a2-4b85-b8df-aa1afa9518e5.png",
      "description": "Is AI coming for our jobs? Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei believes AI could wipe out many white-collar jobs in the next few years. While Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang argues AI will reshape existing roles and create even more jobs than we have now. So which future are we really facing: a job-pocalypse or a jobs transformation?For answers, join The Indicator's Adrian Ma for \"Ask An Economist.\u201d This is a virtual event and live Q&A featuring two economists who've studied this issue: Daron Acemoglu, a Nobel Prize-winning professor at MIT, and Erik Brynjolfsson, a professor at Stanford and director of the Stanford Digital Economy Lab. We\u2019ll also invite you to ask questions and share your thoughts!It's Wednesday, October 28th, at 3:00pm ET, noon PT. This is a Zoom event exclusively for NPR+ and other qualifying supporters. For registration and event details, you can listen to this audio message or check out npr.org/askaneconomist.\u00a0 Support public media with NPR+ and enjoy perks for over 25 podcasts like this one. This show\u2019s perks include sponsor-free listening. Learn more at plus.npr.org."
    },
